/// A crown of painted leaf cards (Crulanda/Leaf) over a trunk. At every clump spot a cluster of two crossed cards fans out
/// from a short bough that grows in from the nearest limb end or the trunk's top; a few small clusters hang low round the rim
/// between them, so the underside is ragged leaf, not a shelf; and a dark squashed core sits at the heart, so the crown is
/// never hollow from below. The cards' union covers about the volume the clumps had (a fan is centred a little past its spot,
/// reaching where the clump's rim was), so a tree's bounds, fade and collider are as before. One mesh for the cards and one
/// for the boughs. Draws only from <paramref name="tr"/>, the tree's own stream, after its trunk and limbs: the zone's is untouched.
/// </summary>
